Step 1: Add the Loki configuration: 
----------------------------------

We'll use the official Grafana Loki Helm chart with Single Binary deploymentmode

First ,add the Grafana Helm repository:

>> helm repo add grafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts

Update the repository: 
>> helm repo update

Check wheather the loki chart is available or not:
>> helm search repo grafana/loki

create loki-values.yaml

Install Loki using the Helm
----------------------------
>> 

helm upgrade --install loki grafana/loki \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --values loki-values.yaml \
  --wait \
  --timeout 10m


After Installation Check : 

>> kubectl get pods -n monitoring
Expected Result: loki-0   2/2   Running   0 restarts

And:

>> kubectl get pvc -n monitoring
Expected Result: storage-loki-0   Bound   10Gi   RWO   standard


___________________________________________________________________________

Install the Grafana/alloy

Step 1: Inspect the available chart
-----------------------------------
>> helm search repo grafana/alloy

Create a alloy-values.yaml

Step 2: Validate the Helm configuaration

>> 
helm template alloy grafana/alloy \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --values alloy-values.yaml \
  > /tmp/alloy-rendered.yaml

Then check : 

>> kubectl get pod -n monitoring
>> kubectl get daemonset alloy -n monitoring

To Check every mounting is correctly working use : 

>> 
kubectl logs -n monitoring daemonset/alloy \
  -c alloy  \
  --tail=60

Or

>>

kubectl logs -n monitoring daemonset/alloy \
  -c alloy \
  --since=5m | grep -Ei 'error|warn|failed|loki|push' | tail -40


If any error occurs correct them and upgrade them: 

helm upgrade --install alloy grafana/alloy \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --values alloy-values.yaml \
  --wait \
  --timeout 10m

